# ACL template for Bem Control's Mosquitto broker.
#
# The real acl.conf (gitignored, lives in mosquitto/certs/acl.conf) is
# generated from this template plus one block per provisioned device,
# appended automatically by backend/src/services/mqttProvisioning.js
# whenever a new ESP32 device is registered.
#
# Run `npm run certs:generate` (from repo root) once to bootstrap both
# files before starting the broker for the first time.

# Backend service account: full access, it's the trust anchor that
# bridges MQTT telemetry into the database and fans out commands.
user bem-backend
topic readwrite #

# --- per-device blocks appended below, one per provisioned device ---
# Example of what gets appended for device "esp32-abc123":
#
# user device-esp32-abc123
# topic write orgs/+/devices/esp32-abc123/telemetry
# topic read orgs/+/devices/esp32-abc123/commands
# topic read orgs/+/devices/esp32-abc123/config
